<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan overnight rates stay high.</title>
<headline>Pakistan overnight rates stay high.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan overnight inter-bank rates remained high on Wednesday due to a shortage of funds in the banking system, dealers said.</p>
<p>Rates opened at 10 percent but climbed to 16 percent due as the State (central) Bank of Pakistan's weekly open market operation (OMO) tightened liquidity, one dealer said.</p>
<p>He said the market ended about two billion rupees short.</p>
<p>The central bank has not yet announced the result of the auction.</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
